# The root .gitignore has `**/vendor/`, because bench/vendor and boot/vendor are
# upstream clones that are read and never committed. desktop/vendor is the
# opposite: miniaudio is vendored *so that* this builds on a clean machine with
# no package manager involved, which only works if it is actually committed.
# Un-ignore the directory here; a nested .gitignore takes precedence over the
# root one for paths beneath it.
!vendor/
!vendor/**

# ... but not the WAV files a run leaves behind. The root .gitignore's *.wav
# rule is still what we want; this line is only here so that the vendor
# negation above cannot accidentally resurrect one.
*.wav
